geneous_fungi","name":"Sanguine Heterogeneous Fungi","icon":"/enemies-icons/Sanguine Heterogeneous Fungi.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"Once a regular sight on the dinner tables of Ursus, found in soups along with cream, black pepper and flour. It has escaped this fate. Its foe is no longer a soup spoon, but crossbow bolts.","abilities":["Continuously channels at a Leak Marker in attack range, causing it to create Leak Sources and gaining increased DEF."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":6250,"atk":130,"def":700,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"sanguine_rockbreaker":{"slug":"sanguine_rockbreaker","name":"Sanguine Rockbreaker","icon":"/enemies-icons/Sanguine Rockbreaker.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"How does moss lift a rock? The Army's researchers tried gene sequencing, chemicals, etc. Until one day its spores fell upon the carcass of a mutated animal. It is quite happy about what happened—people now run away from it screaming. This once insignificant creature has finally earned respect.","abilities":["Splits when first affected by a <Leak Source>."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.75,"stats":{"hp":5000,"atk":500,"def":1700,"res":60,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2.3}},"leak_source":{"slug":"leak_source","name":"Leak Source","icon":"/enemies-icons/Leak Source.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Flying","attackPosition":null,"damageType":["No Damage"],"flavourText":"People would bring tuskbeasts and let them howl at anyone running a fever, believing that their cry would scare away the evil spirits haunting the patient—that is, until the tuskbeasts began running fevers too.","abilities":["Cannot be attacked","Not visible normally; increases ATK when it reveals itself.","Periodically fires a ring of beams that cause the first allied unit hit to take continuous True damage for a period of time, with closer units taking higher damage more frequently. When a beam hits a target, it accelerates the process of revealing the source.","Reveals itself after some time, firing more beams more frequently; leaves the field some time after revealing itself.","Revealed when an Operator is deployed on its tile or the four adjacent tiles; during this period, beams only affect the earliest-deployed Operator nearby; leaves the field after some time and gives all allied Operators SP."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0,"stats":{"hp":100000,"atk":15,"def":0,"res":0,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":0.5}},"roaming_likho":{"slug":"roaming_likho","name":"Roaming 'Likho'","icon":"/enemies-icons/Roaming 'Likho'.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"'Never wake a sleeping Likho'—a saying in Ursus meaning not to stir up trouble where there is none. Also not to approach a sleeping Likho. But perhaps the Likho, herald of misfortune, is coming for Ursus anyway.","abilities":["More likely to be attacked","Creates a <Leak Source> nearby when defeated."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":100000,"atk":1200,"def":0,"res":0,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":4.2}},"angry_shishiga":{"slug":"angry_shishiga","name":"Angry 'Shishiga'","icon":"/enemies-icons/Angry 'Shishiga'.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"When the monsters take to the streets for the first time, their deformed limbs slapping people's homes, the people finally realize what experiments occurred in the secretive underground laboratories. They will no longer be slow, when their potential is fully unleashed.","abilities":["Next attack hits three times when affected by a <Leak Source>."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":12000,"atk":2100,"def":800,"res":25,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":6}},"ama_10":{"slug":"ama_10","name":"AMa-10","icon":"/enemies-icons/AMa-10.webp","rank":"Boss","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"'Protect yourself, AMa-10. Survival is an instinct the living are born with.' At the time, she did not understand what could be worth giving up immortality for.","abilities":["Cannot move or be teleported.","ATK gradually increases when attacking the same target","[Firewall] Has a Firewall around its 8 surrounding tiles; takes greatly reduced Physical and Arts damage from outside the firewall. Allied units cannot be deployed inside the Firewall.","[Refresh] Periodically teleports to the target tile and refreshes the Firewall.","[Information Flood] Releases a 3-tile-wide flood of information in a direction, causing the first unit hit to be stunned and continuously take True damage for a period of time."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":1,"stats":{"hp":90000,"atk":600,"def":1200,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":6}},"ama_10_isomer":{"slug":"ama_10_isomer","name":"AMa-10 Isomer","icon":"/enemies-icons/AMa-10 Isomer.webp","rank":"Boss","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"'Kal'tsit, I hope you can protect the life on this great land.' She will return to us with a promise.","abilities":["Cannot move or be teleported.","ATK gradually increases when attacking the same target","When another AMa-10 Isomer is alive and not in coma, enters a coma when HP reaches 0 and begins regenerating; revive